@defun deleteList (List* list) @arrow{} void
Deletes the elements in List @code{list}.  Also frees @code{list}.
@end defun

@defun lengthList (List* list) @arrow{} int
Returns the number of elements in @code{list}
@end defun

@defun isEmptyList (List* list) @arrow{} bool
Returns @code{true} if List @code{list} is empty, @code{false}
otherwise.
@end defun

@defun findInList (List* list, CString key, int* index index) @arrow{} void*
Searches @code{list} for @code{key}.  If found, it is returned and
@code{*index} is set to its index.  Otherwise, @code{null} is
returned.
@end defun

@defun getListElement (List *list, int index) @arrow{} void*
Gets a specific element from a list.  It is not a copy.
@end defun

@defun appendToList (List* list, const void* element) @arrow{} void
Appends @code{element} to the end of @code{list}, extending the list
by one element.
@end defun

@defun prependToList (List* list, const void* element) @arrow{} void
Prepends @code{element} to the start of @code{list}, pushing all other
elements down by one index.
@end defun

@defun sortList (List*) @arrow{} void
Sorts a list using the list's compare function.
@end defun

@defun searchList (List* list, CString key, int* index) @arrow{} void*
Searches @code{list} for the key @code{key}.  Returns the element and
sets @code{index} to the location of the element.
@end defun

@defun removeFromList (List* list, int index) @arrow{} bool
Remove element having index @code{index} from List @code{list}.  All
subsequent elements are moved up by one.P
@end defun

@defun getAndRemoveFirstListElement (List*) @arrow{} void*
@end defun

@defun initList (List*, CString(*g)(const void*), int(*c)(CString, CString), void(*d)(void*), bool sorted) @arrow{} void
Intiailizes a list.
@end defun

@defun emptyList (List*) @arrow{} void
Removes all elements from a list.
@end defun

@defun copyList (List*, void*(*c)(void*)) @arrow{} List*
Creates a copy of a list.  Requires a copy function to make copies of the list elements.
@end defun

@defun isInList (List*, CString key, int* index) @arrow{} bool
Checks of an element with key @code{key} is in the list.  If found,
@code{index} is set to its location.
@end defun

@defun setListElement (List*, void* element, int index) @arrow{} void
Sets a specific element in a list.
@end defun

@defun insertInList (List*, const void* element, int index) @arrow{} void
Inserts an element into a list at a specified location, moving the
following elements down.  The isSorted flag is not changed.  If an
insertion can cause a sorted list to become unsorted, then the caller
should change the flag to @code{false}.
@end defun

@defun isSortedList (List*) @arrow{} bool
Just checks the sorted flag.
@end defun

@defun isListSorted (List*) @arrow{} bool
Really checks if the list is sorted.
@end defun

@defun uniqueList (List*) @arrow{} void
Removes duplicates from a list.
@end defun

@defun removeFirstListElement (List*) @arrow{} bool
Removes the first element for a list.  Uses the list's delete function.
@end defun

@defun removeLastListElement (List*) @arrow{} bool
Removes the last element from a list.  Uses the list's delete function.
@end defun

@defun iterateList (List*, void(*perform)(void*)) @arrow{} void
Iterates the elements of a list, calling function @code{perform} on
each element.
@end defun

@defun isFirstElementInList (List*, void* element) @arrow{} bool
Checks if @code{element} is the first element of the list.
@end defun

@defun isLastElementInList (List*, void* element) @arrow{} bool
Checks if @code{element} is the last element of the list.
@end defun

@defun getFromList (List*, int index) @arrow{} void*
Returns an indexed element from a list.  The element is not remove from the list.
@end defun

@defun getFirstListElement (List*) @arrow{} void*
Returns the first element from a list.  It is not removed from the list.
@end defun

@defun getLastListElement (List*) @arrow{} void*
Returns the last element from a list.  It is not removed from the list.
@end defun

@defun getAndRemoveLastListElement (List*) @arrow{} void*
Removes the last element from the list and returns it to the caller.
The caller must free it when done.
@end defun

@defun blockOfList (List*) @arrow{} Block*
@end defun

@defun incrReferenceCountList (List *list, CString file, int line, CString function) @arrow{} void
Increments a list's reference count.  The @code{file}, @code{line},
and @code{function} arguments are those of the caller and areused for
debugging reference count issues.

@b{NOTE:} This function is typically not called directly, but instead
via the INCRLISTREFCOUNT macro.
@end defun

@defmac INCRLISTREFCOUNT (list)
Calls the @code{incrReferenceCountList} function supplying the
@code{file}, @code{line}, and @code{function} arguments.
@end defmac

