@section Internal Functions
@subsection block.h / block.c

With the exception of @code{initBlock}, @code{emptyBlock}, and
@code{appendToBlock}, none of these functions are accessed outside of
the @code{DataTypes} library.

From outside the library, the aforementioned three functions are only
called by @code{personKeysFromName} in @file{Gedcom/name.c}.

Additionally, from outside the library, there are three functions that
do not call any of these functions, but do know the internals of the
@code{Block} structure.  They are @code{getRootListFromGNodeList} in
@file{Gedcom/rootlist.c}, @code{interpForList} in
@file{Interp/builtinlist.c}, and @code{showSymbolTable} in
@file{Interp/symboltable.c}.

@defun createBlock (void) @arrow{} Block*
Create an empty Block.
@end defun

@defun initBlock (Block*) @arrow{} void
Initialize an existing Block.
@end defun

@defun deleteBlock (Block*, void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} void
Deallocates the elements of a Block, but not the Block itself.  If a
delete function @code{delete} is supplied, it is called on each
element before the elements are freed.
@end defun

@defun emptyBlock (Block*, void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} void
Removes all the elements in a block.
@end defun

@defun lengthBlock (Block* block) @arrow{} int
Returns the length of a Block @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun isEmptyBlock (Block* block) @arrow{} bool
Returns @code{true} if @code{block} is empty.
@end defun

@defun getBlockElement (Block* block, int index) @arrow{} void*
Returns the @code{index} element from @code{block}.  The caller must
not change it.
@end defun

@defun setBlockElement (Block* block, void* element, void(*delete)(void*), int index) @arrow{} void
Replaces the @code{index} element in @code{block}.  Before
replacement, @code{delete} is called on the element being replaced.
@end defun

@defun findInBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int* index) @arrow{} void*
Returns the element in @code{block} having key @code{key}, if it
exists.  If it is not found, @code{null} is returned.  Uses linear search.
@end defun

@defun findInSortedBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int(*compare)(CString, CString), int* index) @arrow{} void*
Returns the element in @code{block} having key @code{key}, if it
exists.  If it is not found, @code{null} is returned.  Uses binary search.
@end defun

@defun isInBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int* index) @arrow{} bool
If key @code{key} is found in Block @code{block}, returns @code{true}
and sets @code{index} to its index.
Uses linear search.
@end defun

@defun isInSortedBlock (Block*, CString, CString(*g)(const void*), int(*c)(CString, CString), int*) @arrow{} bool
If key @code{key} is found in Block @code{block}, returns @code{true}
and sets @code{index} to its index.
Uses binary search.
@end defun

@defun prependToBlock (Block* block, const void* element) @arrow{} void
Prepends a new element @code{element} to the front of Block @code{block}'s elements.
@end defun

@defun appendToBlock (Block* block, const void* element) @arrow{} void
Appeds a new element @code{element} to the end of Block @code{block}'s elements.
@end defun

@defun insertInBlock (Block* block, const void* element, int index) @arrow{} void
Inserts an element @code{element} into a Block @code{block} at index
@code{index}.  Elements from the given location to the end are shifted
downward.  The Block @code{block} is grown if necessary to accommodate
the new element.
@end defun

@defun removeFromBlock (Block* block, int index, void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} bool
Removes the element at location @code{index} from @code{block}.
Subsequence elements are moved up.  If @code{block} is @code{null} or
@code{index} is out of range, then @code{false} is returned.
Otherwise, @code{true} is returned.
@end defun

@defun removeFromSortedBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*getKey)(const void* a), int(*compare)(CString, CString), void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} bool
Removes an element with key @code{key} from Block @code{block}.  Uses
binary search to find the element and then uses @code{removeFromBlock}
to remove it.
@end defun

@defun removeFromUnsortedBlock (Block*, CString, CString(*g)(const void* a), void(*d)(void*)) @arrow{} bool
Removes an element with key @code{key} from Block @code{block}.  Uses
linear search to find the element and then uses @code{removeFromBlock}
to remove it.
@end defun

@defun removeFirstBlockElement (Block* block, void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} bool
Removes the first element from @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun removeLastBlockElement (Block* block, void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} bool
Removes the last element from @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun sortBlock (Block* block, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int(*compare)(CString, CString)) @arrow{} void
Sorts the elements in @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun isSorted (Block* block, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int(*compare)(CString, CString)) @arrow{} bool
Returns @code{true} if Block @code{block} is currently in sorted order.
@end defun

@defun getFromBlock (Block* block, int index) @arrow{} void*
Returns the Block @code{block} element at index @code{index}.
It is @b{NOT} removed from @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun getFirstBlockElement (Block*) @arrow{} void*
Returns the first element in Block @code{block}.
It is @b{NOT} removed from @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun getLastBlockElement (Block*) @arrow{} void*
Returns the last element in Block @code{block}.
It is @b{NOT} removed from @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun uniqueBlock (Block* block, CString(*getKey)(const void*), void(*delete)(void*)) @arrow{} void
Removes elements with duplicate keys from @code{block}.  The Block
@code{block} must be ordered so that all elements with the same key
are grouped together.
@end defun

@defun copyBlock (Block* block, void*(*copy)(void*)) @arrow{} Block*
Creates and returns a copy of @code{block}.
@end defun

@defun iterateBlock (Block* block, void(*perform)(void*)) @arrow{} void
Iterates over the elements of @code{block} performing an action
@code{perform} on each one.
@end defun

@defun searchBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*getKey)(const void*), int* index) @arrow{} void*
Searches an unsorted Block @code{block} for an element having key
@code{key}.  If found, it is returned and @code{index} is set to its
location.  Otherwise, @code{null} is returned and @code{index} is set
to @code{-1}.  Uses linear search.
@end defun

@defun searchSortedBlock (Block* block, CString key, CString(*g)(const void*), int(*c)(CString, CString), int*) @arrow{} void*
Searches an unsorted Block @code{block} for an element having key
